[Music]  super bowl of caring mobilizes ordinary  people to do extraordinary good in their  local communities  the super bowl of caring started 30  years ago in a church in south carolina  with one prayer on super bowl sunday to  be mindful of those who don't have a  bowl  full of soup to eat the youth at that  church  took that on as a as a challenge and  they asked the question what if  everybody watching the big game just  gave a dollar or one can of food  and if you look at that today that would  be a hundred million dollars in one day  executive director allison reese says  they've raised more than 163 million  dollars to date  a small organization with a large  network  due to the pandemic they began looking  at how technology can assist with this  year's efforts  they created the tackle hunger map you  use the search bar to find  charities in your neighborhood zip code  or city to encourage thinking about  giving locally through churches homeless  shelters pantries and food banks  and most people don't know where their  nearest food charity is  and that's something that we're trying  to address  using our map nobody just says oh i  think i want to open a food pantry that  seems like a good thing to do  every one of them will tell you how  difficult this world is  to manage and how difficult it is to  find the products that are needed  and how difficult it is when one has to  turn someone away  and doesn't have the product that they  need and right now many of our food  charities are having to do that  super bowl of caring doesn't deliver  food directly it acts more like a  catalyst  by infusing the money into the food  charities across the nation  and with next our nation's outreach this  year the nonprofit  hopes you will help raise more than one  million meals

